<urn:atm:triage:finding/DEADCODE-STORAGE-001>
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:correctionNote "quality-mgr (2026-07-27): QA-1 for PR #670 (fix/storage-test-support-cfg @ 453ed008). SqliteWriterLockGuard struct (lib.rs:40-44), its Drop impl (lib.rs:119-124), and hold_sqlite_writer_lock (lib.rs:132-145) now carry #[cfg(any(test, feature = \"test-support\"))], matching the sibling already-gated TestOnlySqliteWriterLockGuard/hold_sqlite_writer_lock_for_test. rust-qa-agent performed a clean rebuild (cargo clean on affected crates + cargo build --release --workspace) and confirmed 0 warnings (both former dead_code warnings at lib.rs:41/130 gone). cargo fmt/clippy -D warnings clean workspace-wide. cargo test --workspace 0 failures, including 19/19 passing in atm-core/tests/mailbox_locking.rs (consumer via atm-runtime-test-support). Workspace-wide duplicate sweep (ruthless-boundary-qa) confirmed no other unguarded writer-lock construct exists. arch-qa confirmed atm-daemon-bootstrap (the only non-dev consumer) does not enable test-support, so no test-only symbols leak into production. All 4 reviewers (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa-agent) independently PASS, 0 blocking findings. CI green 8/8 legs." .